msgid "Sign off translation (human adjudicator)"
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/translation-workflow.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Source content exists in the folio's defaultLocale. A change to source content also triggers this event for staleness re-evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: skills/workflows/translation-workflow.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only lane here that JUDGES. Mechanical translation QA produces candidates — a flagged passage, a terminology miss, a staleness verdict — and a candidate is not a finding until somebody decides it is. This lane is where that decision is made, and it is the lane that signs the translation off, because the actor who resolves a disputed passage is the one who can say the whole is fit to publish. Adjudicator rather than reviewer alone, and the distinction is the accountability: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles. The word is used here because the passage reaching this lane is one where a checker and a translator disagree, and somebody has to choose between them WITH a reason. That reason is the record, not the choice."
msgstr ""

